{
  "origin": "The executor's stop used to land nowhere: `blocked` rendered a gate whose ways out were retry, skip and stop, so an answer rode a retry comment into the re-dispatch and reached no document at all — the one phase with no route to the tiers the specification and the plan already had. On `blocked` the orchestrator now classifies before anything renders, and only a fork the record cannot settle reaches the user, as the task's header, the block in the register, and a gate whose rows are the fork's sides numbered with the recommendation first and Comment. A question the record answers is tier one and gets none of it: a silent corrigendum on the specification from `implementation/{topic}`, the answer landed on the task in flight as the orchestrator's own addition, the executor continued. The no-stop is not a gate mode — it is the block never reaching a gate at all, which is why this walks it with every gate `gated` and the user stopped only where the loop stops anyway. Nothing renders for the block: no result header, no options, no menu; the first the user hears of it is the one line saying what landed.",
